    "result_text": "Done. The full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 2/2 tests passing).\n\n## What I changed\n\nThe `contactPreference` field is a derived response value on `OwnerDto`, which follows the exact same pattern as the existing computed fields (`displayName`, `locality`, `membershipLevel`). Two small, cohesive additions:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 declared a read-only `contactPreference` string property on the `Owner` schema, so the generated DTO gets the field/setter (alongside the other derived fields).\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added one `@Mapping` line to `toOwnerDto`:\n   ```java\n   @Mapping(target = \"contactPreference\",\n       expression = \"java(owner.getEmail() != null && !owner.getEmail().isEmpty() ? \\\"EMAIL\\\" : \\\"PHONE\\\")\")\n   ```\n   This mirrors the exact email null/empty check already used for `membershipLevel`.\n\n## Structural impact\n\nNo function body was grown and no class expanded its logic. The only touched method is the abstract `toOwnerDto` (CC 1), gaining a single annotation line \u2014 the derived value lives entirely in a MapStruct expression rather than in imperative code, so no method's cyclomatic complexity increases. Two files touched, both minimal edits.",
